(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of"] [4 1 "// CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),"] [5 1 "// their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:"] [6 1 "// PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN"] [7 1 "// and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool"] [8 1 "// over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's"] [11 1 "// tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Not built: the local events (set_local_events,"] [12 1 "// get_local_events record nothing), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP, BRANCH*, RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and"] [13 1 "// STOP_ITERATION never fire (settrace's are 219's), DISABLE returned by a callback disables nothing, restart_events is a"] [14 1 "// no-op. CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit)."] [16 1 "// the events' numbers (the bit index of sys.monitoring.events' values)"] [28 2 "// monProfileTool is the legacy profiler's tool (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID)"] [33 1 "// monCallFamily are the events a profiler uses (legacy_tracing.c's for sys.setprofile)"] [37 1 "// monTool is a tool's registration: its name (nil: free), its global events, its callbacks by event."] [42 2 "// native, for the legacy profiler: called in place of cb"] [48 2 "// monEvents is the union of every tool's global events: the hooks' one load"] [50 2 "// monMissing and monDisable are sys.monitoring.MISSING and DISABLE"] [53 2 "// monTracing are the threads running a callback (tstate->tracing); under the GIL"] [55 2 "// monVersion is the interpreter's instrumentation version (queue 274b, the C API's PyMonitoring_EnterScope): raised"] [56 2 "// when a tool's global events change (monSeen: the events at the last change), as _PyMonitoring_SetEvents does"] [61 1 "// monUpdate recomputes monEvents, and breakMonitor in the eval breaker: a frame's start checks the breaker alone, so"] [62 1 "// its PY_START costs nothing while no tool has an event."] [80 1 "// monFire calls the tools' callbacks of event ev with args; the first error is returned (raised where the event is)."] [116 1 "// monEnter is a frame's start in runFrames: PY_THROW for an exception thrown into a generator's frame, PY_START for a"] [117 1 "// frame at its first instruction, else PY_RESUME."] [136 1 "// monLeave is a frame's return of v in runFrames: PY_YIELD when it is suspended, else PY_RETURN."] [148 1 "// monUnwind is a frame left by exc (PY_UNWIND); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [161 1 "// monCall is CALL before a call of callable from f, arg0 its first argument (self for a method) or nil."] [172 1 "// monCReturn is C_RETURN or C_RAISE after a call of callable, not a Python function, from f: the call's result, or a"] [173 1 "// callback's error."] [191 1 "// monCallC is a call of a callable that is not a Python function from f with monitoring on: CALL, the call, then"] [192 1 "// C_RETURN or C_RAISE."] [205 1 "// isPyFunction is whether a call of o runs a Python frame (a function, or a bound method of one): no C events."] [218 1 "// the legacy profiler (sys.setprofile): each thread's function, and how many threads have one"] [233 1 "// setProfile is _PyEval_SetProfile for t: fn None removes it."] [243 1 "// profileCFunc is the C function a CALL's callable stands for (legacy_tracing.c's sys_profile_call_or_return): a"] [244 1 "// built-in function or method itself, a method descriptor bound to its first argument; nil for any other callable."] [258 1 "// builtinOwner is the type in arg0's type's MRO whose dict holds b (a method descriptor's d_type), or nil."] [271 1 "// profileEvent is the legacy tool's callback: the thread's profile function called as (frame, event, arg); an error"] [272 1 "// removes it (sys.setprofile(None)) and is raised."] [306 1 "// newMonitoringModule is sys.monitoring."] [461 1 "// monCallSite is a call site's monitoring (queue 220): CALL fired; a callable that is no Python function called here"] [462 1 "// with C_RETURN or C_RAISE after it (done true, its result); a Python function's call left to the site (done false)."] [479 1 "// callStackMon is callStack's monitoring: monCallSite over the call's callable and arguments on f's stack, which a C"] [480 1 "// callable's call pops."] [505 1 "// The C API's view of the monitors (queue 274b; Python/instrumentation.c's PyMonitoring_EnterScope and"] [506 1 "// capi_call_instrumentation, CPython 3.14.10): the C half is pyctypes' (capi_monitoring.go)."] [508 1 "// monEventNames are instrumentation.c's event_names, by event number."] [513 1 "// MonitoringVersion is the instrumentation version PyMonitoring_EnterScope compares with a scope's."] [516 1 "// MonitoringTools is _Py_GlobalMonitors' tools[ev]: the tools whose global events have ev. An extension's tool's events"] [517 1 "// as set_events stores them (monitoring_set_events_impl: BRANCH as BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT, C_RETURN and C_RAISE"] [518 1 "// left out, they follow CALL)."] [536 1 "// MonitoringEventName is event_names[ev]."] [544 1 "// MonitoringCall is call_one_instrument for the C API: tool's callback of ev called with args (0: none, or it returned;"] [545 1 "// 1: it returned DISABLE), with the thread's tracing count up. A native tool (the legacy profiler) has no callback for"] [546 1 "// an extension's events."] [570 1 "// MonitoringClearCallback clears tool's callback of ev (capi_call_instrumentation's \"Callback removed\")."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[91 41] [102 21] [153 79] [154 29] [185 78] [198 40] [207 27] [211 36] [251 36] [265 25] [297 20] [354 29] [391 28] [408 22] [435 13] [435 29] [468 40] [488 40] [558 20]]} (go/file "monitoring.go" :imports [])

;; sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of
;; CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),
;; their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:
;; PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN
;; and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool
;; over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool.
;;
;; Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's
;; tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Not built: the local events (set_local_events,
;; get_local_events record nothing), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP, BRANCH*, RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and
;; STOP_ITERATION never fire (settrace's are 219's), DISABLE returned by a callback disables nothing, restart_events is a
;; no-op. CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit).


